# Match the existing codebase

Before adding files or inventing a pattern, read nearby code and follow it. Do not introduce a new folder layout, naming style, library, or abstraction when the current one already covers the case.

## Architecture

Turborepo + npm workspaces. Apps do not import each other.

| Workspace | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/web` | Next.js App Router (customer) |
| `apps/admin` | Vite + React Router (admin) |
| `packages/ui` (`@repo/ui`) | Shared primitives and tokens |
| `packages/types` (`@repo/types`) | Shared API/domain types |

- Shared UI: `npx shadcn@latest add <name> -c packages/ui`, then `import { Button } from "@repo/ui/components/button"`.
- Screens and feature composition stay in the app, not in `@repo/ui`.
- Shared request/response types go in `@repo/types`. Feature-only types and Zod schemas stay in the feature.

## Feature structure

Routes stay thin. Product code lives in feature modules and is imported through the feature barrel.

```text
apps/web/features/<name>/
  index.ts                 # public exports only
  components/              # PascalCase: LoginForm.tsx
  hooks/                   # camelCase: useLogin.ts
  services/                # auth.service.ts
  schemas.ts
```

Admin mirrors this under `apps/admin/src/features/<name>/`.

```tsx
// GOOD — page imports the feature public API
import { LoginForm } from "@/features/auth";

// BAD — page reaching into feature internals, or a new top-level folder
import { LoginForm } from "@/features/auth/components/LoginForm";
```

- Features import `@repo/ui` and `@repo/types`.
- Features do not import another feature's internals or `app/`.
- Inside a feature, use relative imports (`../hooks/useLogin`).

## Coding standards

- TypeScript, functional components, named exports. Default export only for Next.js `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.
- `"use client"` only when the file needs client APIs (forms, motion, hooks).
- Forms: `react-hook-form` + `zodResolver` + `Controller`. Mutations: TanStack Query hooks wrapping `*.service.ts` that call `api` from `lib/axios`.
- Style with existing Tailwind tokens and `cn` from `@repo/ui/lib/utils`. Keep `--radius: 0` (no rounded controls, no box-shadow highlights).
- Prettier: double quotes, semicolons, trailing commas, printWidth 80.
- Use npm, not pnpm or yarn.
